    ; ═══ transformers/declarations — THE DECLARATION EMITTER (slice 250) ═════════
    ;
    ; transform.go whole, with util.go, tracker.go and diagnostics.go, as one
    ; tagged transformer (TransformerTagDeclaration, the `dt_*` family) with six
    ; sub-visitors under `dt_visitor(sub)` — the reference's binding-name,
    ; nested-expression, export-stripping, this-property, CJS-export-assignment
    ; and declare-stripping closures (§3.41's shape). The symbol tracker and the
    ; state it shares with the transformer are fields of THIS record: the
    ; reference splits them into two structs only so the node builder can be
    ; handed the tracker, and the builder is a stop here. The `getSymbolAccessibilityDiagnostic`
    ; func value is a TAG plus a node (§3.18, `dt_diag_kind`/`dt_diag_node`), and
    ; a diagnostic is (pos, end, code) as everywhere in this port — what the
    ; driver reads off the list is its LENGTH, because the reference skips the
    ; .d.ts of a file whose declaration emit reports.
    ;
    ; ★★★ EVERY NODE-BUILDER ENTRY POINT IS A SAID STOP, `node-builder <kind>`:
    ; CreateTypeOfDeclaration, CreateReturnTypeOfSignatureDeclaration,
    ; CreateTypeParametersOfSignatureDeclaration, CreateTypeOfExpression,
    ; CreateLateBoundIndexSignatures' late-bound half, TryJSTypeNodeToTypeNode
    ; and the enum arm of CreateLiteralConstValue. A declaration whose type the
    ; emitter must INFER is UNPORTED rather than written wrong; one that is
    ; annotated passes through. The builder is the next chapter.
    ;
    ; ★ The parser keeps a file's lib references by NAME only; a `preserve="true"`
    ; reference directive (path, types or lib) is not recorded and therefore not
    ; re-emitted — the one deviation this slice knows of.

    function the_binder(this) @ret_param_0 true @deep true returns ref[Binder] linked

    ; the visitors the reference builds per closure, made on first use (§3.5jm)
    procedure dt_visitor(mutable this, sub: int) @ret_param_0 true @deep true returns ref[NodeVisitor] linked

